T}:T{
.sp
Change with
T}
.T&
lt lt lt.
T{
.sp
\f(CI.\fP matches newline
T}:T{
.sp
no
T}:T{
.sp
\f(CBPCRE2_\:DOTALL\fP
T}
T{
.sp
\f(CI[^a]\fP matches newline
T}:T{
.sp
yes
T}:T{
.sp
not changeable
T}
T{
.sp
\f(CI$\fP matches newline at end
T}:T{
.sp
yes
T}:T{
.sp
\f(CBPCRE2_\:DOLLAR_\:ENDONLY\fP
T}
T{
.sp
\f(CI$\fP matches newline in middle
T}:T{
.sp
no
T}:T{
.sp
\f(CBPCRE2_\:MULTILINE\fP
T}
T{
.sp
\f(CI^\fP matches newline in middle
T}:T{
.sp
no
T}:T{
.sp
\f(CBPCRE2_\:MULTILINE\fP
T}
.TE
.sp
.sp
This is the equivalent table for a POSIX\-compatible pattern matcher:
.TS
allbox tab(:);
ltB ltB ltB.
